SUMMARY:Music Appreciation from the 1950s\, 1960s and 1970s Social Event!
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin us for a fun and interactive Sunday night celebrating the music of
  the **’50s\, ’60s and ’70s**! We’ll listen to great songs from al
 l three decades\, share memories and talk about the artists and sounds tha
 t made each era memorable.\nㅤ\n\n* **The ’50s** brought us early rock 
 ’n’ roll\, rockabilly and doo-wop\, with artists like Elvis Presley\, 
 Chuck Berry and Buddy Holly.\n* **The ’60s** gave us the Beatles\, the B
 each Boys and the Supremes\, along with the sounds of the British Invasion
 \, surf pop and Motown.\n* **The ’70s** took us from Gordon Lightfoot an
 d Fleetwood Mac to Stevie Wonder and the Bee Gees\, with singer-songwriter
 s\, classic rock\, soul and disco.\n\nㅤ\nWhether you grew up with these 
 songs or discovered them years later\, everyone is encouraged to join in. 
 Bring a favourite song or album to talk about\, share a memory\, or come h
 ear a few forgotten gems and meet other people who love music.\nㅤ\n*We
 ’ll be joined by my other social groups too\, so we can look forward to 
 a friendly crowd and good conversation!*\nㅤ\n*We’ll be in the back din
 ing area at The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub\, 1999 Avenue Road\, roughly six bl
 ocks north of Lawrence Avenue and south of the 401. When you arrive\, ask 
 the bartender or wait staff for Steve’s event.*\nㅤ\nSincerely\,\nSteve
  Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\nㅤ\n\n***\n\n### Event Details\n\n**About Yo
 ur Host**\nSteve Flemming has been a DJ since the early 2000s and has a li
 felong passion for music\, especially from the 1960s through the 1990s. Hi
 s father was also a DJ during the ’70s and ’80s\, so music was a big p
 art of Steve’s life growing up. He enjoys sharing great songs and bringi
 ng people together through music.\nㅤ\n**Event Fee**\n**$5 per person** (
 HST included). Pay cash at the door or send an e-transfer to [steveflemmin
 g11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com).\n*No extra charge for th
 ose attending the earlier event.*\nㅤ\n**Friendly Reminders**\n\n* Please
  arrive anytime between **6:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.**\, if possible.\n* You
 ’re welcome to arrive earlier. Please ask for Steve when you arrive.\n* 
 The Pheasant offers a dinner menu and food specials.\n* To help support th
 e venue\, please purchase at least one beverage or appetizer upon arrival.
 \n\nㅤ\n**Parking and Transportation**\nThere’s street parking along Av
 enue Road and free parking on nearby residential side streets where permit
 ted.\nㅤ\nThe venue is approximately a 15–20-minute walk from Lawrence 
 subway station at Yonge and Lawrence. You can also take a bus or Uber from
  the station.\nㅤ\n[The Pheasant: A Firkin Pub website](https://www.firki
 npubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)
