SUMMARY:Friday Night After Party with Retro Crush! ('80s Tribute Band) 
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nHello everyone\,\n\n
 Join us for a fun **Friday Night After Party at Smoke Show BBQ & Brew** on
  **Friday\, December 4**\, featuring **Retro Crush\, an ’80s tribute ban
 d!** Enjoy live ’80s favourites\, dancing\, drinks and friendly company 
 in a casual\, lively atmosphere. Come on your own or bring a friend\, and 
 join us on the dance floor!\n\n*Joined by my other groups too :)*\n\n\\*I'
 ll be at the front door when you arrive (ask for Steve's group)\n\nEvent d
 etails below.\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n──
 ──────────────────────\n**EVEN
 T DETAILS**\n**Friday Night After Party with Retro Crush! ('80s Tribute Ba
 nd)**\n\n* 🎸 Live music by Retro Crush\, an ’80s tribute band\n* 🎶
  ’80s favourites and dance-floor hits\n* 💃 Dancing\n* 🍻 Drinks and
  food available\n* 🎉 Socializing and good times\n* 👋 New members and
  solo attendees welcome\n\nThis is a social night first and foremost. Come
  meet some people\, enjoy the music\, have a drink\, hit the dance floor\,
  or do all four!\n──────────────────
 ──────\n**FRIENDLY REMINDERS**\n\n* Please be respectful and f
 riendly toward everyone attending.\n* If you RSVP\, please do your best to
  attend or update your RSVP if your plans change.\n* Food and beverages ar
 e purchased individually from the venue.\n* Please drink responsibly and a
 rrange safe transportation home.\n* Ask for Steve and the Meetup group whe
 n you arrive.\n* Most importantly\, come ready for some great music and a 
 fun Friday night!\n\n**Event fee**\n$10 at the door (cash only) or in adva
 nce by e-transfer to [steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gm
 ail.com).\n**Arrival time**\nPlease arrive between **8:30 p.m. and 10:00 p
 .m.** Mention that you’re with Steve’s group when you arrive.\n**Parki
 ng**\nStreet parking is available\, with free parking in the residential a
 rea and on Mt. Pleasant north of Eglinton.
