DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nGood day everyone\,\
 n\nJoin us for **Movie Night with Friends – I Play Rocky!** A fun and re
 laxed Saturday evening of meeting new people\, enjoying some friendly conv
 ersation and catching a movie together at the cinema!\n\nWe'll begin by ga
 thering downstairs before heading up to the VIP lounge\, where everyone ca
 n mingle and enjoy optional food\, cocktails\, wine or beer before we sett
 le in to watch **I Play Rocky**.\n\nWhether you're a movie enthusiast or s
 imply looking for an enjoyable evening out with friendly company\, we'd lo
 ve to have you join us!\n\n*We'll also be joined by members of my other so
 cial groups\, so we can anticipate a wonderful turnout with plenty of frie
 ndly people to meet!*\n\n**Event Details Below:**\n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve 
 Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n[https://www.meetup.com/soulcity/](https://www
 .meetup.com/soulcity/)\n\n***\n\n## Details of Event:\n\n**Movie Night wit
 h Friends – I Play Rocky!**\n**What Can You Expect?**\n\n* A friendly so
 cial gathering with fellow movie lovers.\n* Time to mix and mingle in the 
 cinema's VIP lounge before the movie.\n* Optional food\, wine\, beer and c
 ocktails available for purchase.\n* An enjoyable evening watching *I Play 
 Rocky* together on the big screen!\n\n**About the Movie:**\n*I Play Rocky*
  tells the inspiring true story behind the making of one of Hollywood's mo
 st beloved films. Before Sylvester Stallone became a household name\, he w
 as a struggling young actor with a dream and a screenplay he believed in. 
 Despite repeated rejection from Hollywood executives\, Stallone refused to
  sell his script unless he could play Rocky Balboa himself. Facing financi
 al hardship and seemingly impossible odds\, he risked everything to bring 
 his vision to life. Starring Anthony Ippolito as the young Stallone and di
 rected by Peter Farrelly\, the film explores determination\, ambition and 
 the courage to believe in yourself. It's an uplifting story about the ulti
 mate underdog who created one of cinema's most unforgettable underdogs.\n\
 n**Event Fee:**\n**$4 per person in advance**\n**$5 per person on the day*
 *\n**Payment Options:**\n\n* **Cash:** $5 per person\, payable to Steve at
  the event.\n* **E-transfer:** $4 per person\, payable in advance to **[st
 eveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:steveflemming11@gmail.com)**.\n\nPlease in
 clude your name with your e-transfer so your payment can be easily identif
 ied.\n*Please note: The event fee is for organizing the social gathering. 
 Movie tickets\, food and drinks are purchased separately.*\n\n***\n\n**Dat
 e\, Time and Location:**\n**Date:** Saturday\, December 5th\, 2026\n**Arri
 val Time:** Please arrive between **5:45 p.m. and 6:00 p.m.**\n**Location:
 ** Cineplex Cinemas Yonge-Eglinton and VIP\, Toronto\n**Meeting Point:**\n
 We'll meet **downstairs in front of the arcade games** between 5:45 p.m. a
 nd 6:00 p.m.\nSimply look for Steve and the group!\nOnce everyone has gath
 ered\, we'll head upstairs together to the **VIP lounge** for some sociali
 zing and optional food and drinks before the movie begins.\n\n***\n\n**Fri
 endly Reminders:**\n\n* Please arrive between 5:45 p.m. and 6:00 p.m. so w
 e can gather before heading upstairs.\n* Food and drinks in the VIP area a
 re entirely optional and purchased individually.\n* Movie admission is sep
 arate from the social event fee (We will purchase our tickets together so 
 we can all sit together)\n\n***\n\n**Come enjoy a fun Saturday evening of 
 movies\, mingling and great company!**
